decision_conditions:
Condition : 8 - The externally illuminated fascia advertisement hereby permitted shall comply with the following terms:

(a)	Between the hours of sunset and 23:00, the intensity of the illumination of the advertisement shall not exceed 300 cd/m2;
(b)	Between the hours of 23:00 and sunrise, the intensity of the illumination of the advertisement shall not exceed 300 cd/m2;
(c)	The advertisement shall be fitted with a light intensity monitoring censor to ensure the illuminance intensity is dimmable to take account of ambient light conditions and comply with the maximum recommended lighting intensity; 
(d)	The advertisement shall not display any moving, or apparently moving, images; 
(e)	Any change in the advertisement display shall be instantaneous;
(f)	The advertisements displayed shall not change more frequently than once every 10 seconds.

Reason: In the interests of amenity and highway safety.

Condition : 9 - The non-illuminated projecting advertisement panel hereby permitted shall comply with the following terms:

(a)	The advertisement shall not display any moving, or apparently moving, images; 
(b)	Any change in the advertisement display shall be instantaneous;
(c)	The advertisements displayed shall not change more frequently than once every 10 seconds.

Reason: In the interests of amenity and highway safety.
